# Project Architecture

## 1. Guiding Principles

- Runtime source → `src/`. Tests → `tests/`. No loose files at project root.
- File names: **kebab-case**. Class names: **PascalCase**.
- Only `main.ts` and `app.module.ts` directly in `src/`. Other `src/*.ts` → **violation**.
- Ambiguous placement → **stop and ask**.

---

## 2. Top-Level Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts / app.module.ts
├── base/              # Shared utilities (no feature-module deps)
├── config-module/     # Env config + validation (typed ConfigService, never raw process.env)
├── health-check/      # Health/monitoring APIs only
└── <feature-module>/
tests/
├── arch/              # Dependency rule tests
├── base/              # Shared test infra (mocks, containers, seeders) — no test cases
└── e2e/               # <subject>.e2e-spec.ts
```

---

## 3. `src/base/` — Shared Utilities

If a feature module utility is imported by another feature module → **move to `base/`** (flag cross-import as violation).

| Directory | Contents |
|---|---|
| `decorators/` | Global decorators (`@CurrentUser()`, `@Public()`) used by 2+ modules |
| `enums/` | Cross-module enums |
| `exceptions/http/` | Base `client.exception.ts` (4xx) and `server.exception.ts` (5xx) + global filter |
| `validations/` | Reusable pipes and class-validator decorators |
| `interfaces/` | Cross-module TS interfaces |
| `interceptors/` | Global interceptors |
| `types/` | Shared TS utility types |
| `helpers/` | Pure functions (no DI, no side effects) |
| `<technology>/` | Tech-specific utils (e.g. `rtc/`, `kafka/`) — tech decorators live here |

All exceptions must extend `client.exception.ts` or `server.exception.ts`.

---

## 4. Feature Modules

One directory per feature. One `<name>.module.ts` — no sub-modules. Create subdirectories only when needed.

```
src/<module-name>/
├── <module-name>.module.ts
├── controllers/          # HTTP REST
├── resolvers/            # GraphQL
├── gateways/             # WebSocket
├── dtos/                 # See DTO structure below
├── entities/             # DB schemas
├── enums/                # Module-specific enums
├── services/             # Business logic
├── helpers/              # Pure functions (no DI)
├── queues/               # <name>.processor.ts (consumer) + <name>.event-publisher.ts
├── exceptions/
│   ├── client/           # 4xx — extend client.exception.ts
│   └── server/           # 5xx — extend server.exception.ts
└── tests/                # Unit tests (<subject>.spec.ts)
```

### DTO Structure & Naming

```
dtos/
├── controller/ (requests/ + responses/)    # HTTP — scope: rest
├── queue/      (requests/ + responses/)    # Kafka — scope: mq
├── ws/         (requests/ + responses/)    # WebSocket — scope: ws
└── service/    (requests/ + responses/)    # Service-layer — no scope
```

**Naming:** `{subject}.{request|response}.{scope}.dto.ts` (endpoint) or `{subject}.{request|response}.dto.ts` (service).
Scopes: `rest`, `ws`, `gql`, `mq`. Only endpoint-layer DTOs get class-validator decorators.

### Services

May import: own entities/helpers/queues, other module services (exported), `base/`.
Must NOT import: controllers, resolvers, gateways, endpoint-layer DTOs.

### Exceptions Naming

`{subject}.{reason}.{client|server}.exception.ts` — e.g. `user.not-found.client.exception.ts`. Subdirectory must match suffix.

---

## 5. Dependency Rules

| Layer | May import from |
|---|---|
| controllers/resolvers/gateways | Own services, own layer DTOs, `base/` |
| services | Own entities/helpers/queues(publishers), other module services, `base/` |
| queues/processors | Own services, `dtos/queue/requests/`, `base/` |
| queues/publishers | `dtos/queue/responses/`, `base/` |
| helpers | `base/` only |
| dtos | Other module DTOs, `base/enums/`, `base/types/` |
| entities | `base/` only |

**Forbidden (flag as violation):**
- Controllers importing entities, queues, or other-module internals
- Services importing endpoint-layer DTOs or controllers
- Services importing `KafkaProducerService` directly — all Kafka publishing MUST go through a dedicated `<name>.event-publisher.ts` in `queues/`. Services call the publisher, never the producer.
- Any module importing `other-module/helpers/` (move to base) or `other-module/exceptions/`

**Cross-module allowed:** other services (via exports), other entities (only for DB relationships, sparingly), other DTOs, other enums.

---

## 6. Naming Cheat Sheet

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Module | `<name>.module.ts` | `user.module.ts` |
| Controller | `<name>.controller.ts` | `chat.controller.ts` |
| Audience Controller | `<audience>.<name>.controller.ts` | `admin.chat.controller.ts` |
| Service | `<name>.service.ts` | `user-profile.service.ts` |
| Entity | `<name>.entity.ts` | `user.entity.ts` |
| Enum | `<name>.enum.ts` | `user-subscription.enum.ts` |
| Helper | `<name>.helper.ts` | `date-format.helper.ts` |
| Kafka Consumer | `<name>.processor.ts` | `user.processor.ts` |
| Kafka Publisher | `<name>.event-publisher.ts` | `user.event-publisher.ts` |
| Endpoint DTO | `<subject>.<req\|res>.<scope>.dto.ts` | `create-user.request.rest.dto.ts` |
| Service DTO | `<subject>.<req\|res>.dto.ts` | `create-user.request.dto.ts` |
| Exception | `<subject>.<reason>.<client\|server>.exception.ts` | `edit.not-allowed.client.exception.ts` |
| Unit test | `<subject>.spec.ts` | `user.service.spec.ts` |
| E2E test | `<subject>.e2e-spec.ts` | `user.e2e-spec.ts` |
| Decorator/Interceptor/Pipe/Filter | `<name>.<type>.ts` | `current-user.decorator.ts` |
